 of functors\n<MATH_0005>\ncorresponds to a unique morphism <MATH_0006>.\nWe omit the verification that <MATH_0007> is a functor and that\nit is right adjoint to <MATH_0008>.\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d1b7528fb9c374aa09616661eb4b7b60babd2aafecbe080f5bfa459da85fbaa8", "unit_id": "inventory:categories:0A8B:proof/0001"}, "state": "READY"}, "inventory:categories:0FWV:proof/0001": {"context_hash": "sha256:061e43e2104421c823ffb12b36fe6b2400dda11be079ccb8aa18331afd45168d", "inventory_id": "inventory:categories:0FWV:proof/0001", "kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 121452, "byte_start": 120742, "file": "categories.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:d1788590df13e7105215b906a52a008a9b322bf527a9a97d0ec0a957d1cc2cd0", "line_end": 3437, "line_start": 3419}, "owner_tag": "0FWV", "parent_tag": "0036", "semantic_path": "proof/0001", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0036", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$u \\circ v$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$Y$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0005": "$$\n\\Mor(X,Y) \\to \\Mor(v(X),v(Y)) \\to \\Mor(u(v(X)), u(v(Y)))\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$v$", "MATH_0007": "$u$", "MATH_0008": "$v$", "MATH_0009": "$$\n\\Mor(v(X), v(Y)) \\to \\Mor(u(v(X)), u(v(Y))) \\to \\Mor(u(v(X)), Y)\n$$", "MATH_0010": "$u(v(Y)) \\to Y$", "MATH_0011": "$\\Mor(v(X), v(Y)) \\to \\Mor(u(v(X)), u(v(Y)))$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{proof}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{proof}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7d34fde23fabb73406d42b55bd5e8d915f60bebe0a7315952a43cbe2c4a3da41", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:35727c498151b3505f2d0efdb006e237eaf88ac66c463160dc9cae7c0cb83295", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nProof of (2). Assume <MATH_0001> is fully faithful.\nSay we have <MATH_0002>, <MATH_0003> in <MATH_0004>.\nThen the natural composite map\n<MATH_0005>\nis a bijection, so <MATH_0006> is at least faithful. To show full faithfulness,\nwe must show that the second map above is injective.\nBut the adjunction between <MATH_0007> and <MATH_0008> says that\n<MATH_0009>\nis a bijection, where the first map is natural one and\nthe second map comes from the counit <MATH_0010> of the adjunction.\nSo this says that\n<MATH_0011>\nis also injective, as wanted. The proof of (1) is dual to this.\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3e5550c7c6b3f87b7de1ca71e7f829de944239164534973562039eccd894c373", "unit_id": "inventory:categories:0FWV:proof/0001"}, "state": "READY"}, "reference:categories-definition-adjoint": {"context_hash": "sha256:3feb00be12f554bc63df73e97f6a355b7e0fe3431f77b3326616c4e661c423fa", "kind": "locked-English-reference", "location": {"byte_end": 118329, "byte_start": 117870, "file": "categories.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:3d4edfd460e9abd34b6ed635af88a1d242927e7fef432173b327a4c0cc3f262f", "line_end": 3357, "line_start": 3343}, "owner_tag": "0037", "parent_tag": "0036", "requested_label": "categories-definition-adjoint", "requested_tag": "0037", "semantic_path": "definition/0001", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0036", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{definition-adjoint}", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0003": "$u : \\mathcal{C} \\to \\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0004": "$v : \\mathcal{D} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$u$", "MATH_0006": "$v$", "MATH_0007": "$v$", "MATH_0008": "$u$", "MATH_0009": "$$\n\\Mor_\\mathcal{D}(u(X), Y)\n\\longrightarrow\n\\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(X, v(Y))\n$$", "MATH_0010": "$X \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0011": "$Y \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{D})$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{definition}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{definition}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0